findings.detail_md:
Pure predicate evaluation over the simulated tree (no git write, no exploit):

- pre-fix rule (head or first parent, one file total) -> REFUSES the ship verdict `9c3fc0f8...` — the LOW CWE-841 the superseded verdict recorded;
- post-fix rule over `(head, first parent, origin/develop tip)` -> no violation;
- post-fix + a second file naming the SAME live sha -> the excess file is REFUSED;
- post-fix + a verdict naming an unreviewed sha (`dddd…`) -> REFUSED.

The doctor's input is `discover_handoff_paths`, which returns `sorted(root.glob(...))`, so duplicate reporting is deterministic rather than filesystem-order dependent.

Patterns applied to `git diff e8ddf085..HEAD | grep '^+'`:

- `(password|passwd|secret|token|api_key|apikey|private_key)\s*[=:]\s*['\"][^'\"]{6,}` — 0 hits;
- `BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY` — 0 hits;
- `AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|xox[baprs]-|sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\.` — 0 hits;
- `/home/<user>|/Users/|192.168.|10.x.x.x|\.local\b|<operator id>|<user>@` — 0 hits.

The two new `BUGS.jsonl` lines were read in full and are correctly redacted: they name only repo-relative module paths and symbols, CLI verbs, bug slugs and law section numbers. Software-integrity note (OWASP A08): this delta edits an agent-instruction asset (`public/skills/dd-gitflow-default/SKILL.md`) and re-records its sha256 in `public/entities/behavior-map.json`; `public doctor` returns `[ok] entities-derivation`, so the instruction change is accounted for by the integrity record rather than drifting silently.
